From: MiaAI-Lab <MiaAI-Lab@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 01:36:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] glm: DSpark tap capture on glm_moe_dsa's one residual stream,
 and TF_GLM_TAP_DUMP

Taps gains a dsa mode (hidden size of the one bf16 stream): after 0-based layers 1, 19, 38, 57, 74 (the inputs of
RedHatAI/GLM-5.3-speculator.dspark's aux_hidden_state_layer_ids 2, 20, 39, 58, 75) each row's whole residual is
copied into its slot of [rows][5][hidden] (cuMemcpy2DAsync). wholeDsa taps after the layer's second reduce instead
of refusing (DFlash2's 4-stream taps still refuse), and a tapped chunk runs whole (no two-halves path).

TF_GLM_TAP_DUMP=<file> (glm_moe_dsa, no drafter): every rank taps its prompt chunks (the same collectives on all
ranks); rank 0 appends a record a chunk ("TAPS", i64 start, i32 rows, i32 hidden, i32 ids, bf16 taps) for the
NumPy twin (scripts/tests/dspark_twin.py).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
